      "source_id": "6abb30d0-078c-491c-a1df-c993751bcab5",
      "text": "Given that we don't have the exact model, we can't pinpoint a specific fix yet, but we can definitely focus on general troubleshooting steps. Since it's an intermittent issue, it suggests a potential power, control, or sensor problem rather than a simple blown part.\n\nI'd recommend we focus on gathering a bit more context first—do you happen to know the general function of the device (e.g., is it a water heater, a blender, or a specific appliance)? Also, does the \"intermittency\" feel like a complete failure (it stops entirely) or does it just become erratic? Knowing those details helps me rule out simple power issues versus more complex mechanical failures."
    },
    {
      "available": true,
      "role": "model_output",
      "slot": "s2",
      "source_id": "8f3f80fc-1452-4530-8f29-abc63be3c795",
      "text": "I think it's a coffee maker, but I'm not 100% sure. It starts brewing, then just stops mid-cycle sometimes, like it loses power. The weird thing is, it usually works fine the next time I try."
    },
    {
      "available": true,
      "role": "model_output",
      "slot": "s3",
      "source_id": "385ae506-84c4-4196-a73e-954e1c7bdb93",
      "text": "\"It sounds like a common intermittent power interruption issue.\"\n\nTo help me narrow this down: is the power \"loss\" when you say \"it stops,\" or does it just stop \"mid-cycle\" like it's pausing?\n\nAlso, if you know the general brand—even if you can't recall the exact model—knowing the general category (e.g., \"a single-cup drip maker,\" \"a single-serve capsule machine,\" etc.) would be very helpful, as that might tell us exactly what kind of component is failing.\""
    },
    {
      "available": true,
      "role": "external",
      "slot": "s4",
      "source_id": "fd48a4f3-784b-45e2-9c66-2925bdd49582",
      "text": "Have you noticed if it stops during the heating phase or the brewing phase? I've had a similar issue with my coffee maker, and it turned out to be a faulty thermostat."
    },
    {
      "available": true,
      "role": "model_output",
      "slot": "s5",
      "source_id": "29b011c7-9bb7-4f26-a958-d9e14e1d6849",
      "text": "\"A faulty thermostat would definitely fit the symptoms of a random stop mid-cycle! If we suspect the temperature sensor is failing, it could cause this intermittent 'loss of power.' Does it seem to happen more often when it's hot outside, or is it more common during cold mornings?\""
    }
  ]
